{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 8, :comments ["<b>The word ויגוע.</b> The departure of the spirit from the body in a single moment without suffering or delay. Note that it says, \"ויאסף רגליו אל המטה\" (Genesis 49:3), and immediately he expired. Now every גויעה is death, but not every death is גויעה; therefore in the Flood it is written ויגוע (Genesis 7:21)." "<b>And the meaning of \"and Abraham died\"</b> is that he died in a good old age." "<b>And was gathered to his people.</b> Some say this refers to the dignity of the soul, for while it is occupied with the body it is like a separated part, and when it separates from the body it is gathered — the dignity — to its people. And some say this is the way of language, and the meaning concerns his going in the way of his fathers, as though he joins them. So too, \"and you shall come to your fathers in peace\" (Genesis 15:15)."], :book :genesis, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 25, :notes {0 "Genesis 49:3 is actually 49:33 in standard chapter numbering; the verse citation as given in the source is preserved."}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"] ["Piotrkow, 1907-1911" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH990020973480205171/NLI"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:45:47.273948278Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}